      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Finite algebra relations for the prescribed polynomial surjection and finite kernel for a finite module surjecting onto a finitely presented quotient; no Noetherian assumption on the original ring."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD2",
      "block_sha256": "39f7d24eeda89acb71f36a0f4af1d46e8a1bfb156ff8033118134329f76b4b31",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Explicit projective splitting gives the correctly sized generalized inverse modulo the actual chart kernel, using the supplied module and semilinear map."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD3",
      "block_sha256": "3d1ef81aea81a14da2113e482cd5f106623ecc64673dae1c3dd0d2d5641a90a1",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "All three finite matrix certificates and the formal-smooth quotient are constructed on the original chart."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD4",
      "block_sha256": "369c87a77a71da5a176d370e4ea222c58b211083521ca6a0fef6753e25cbec8c",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Both directions of the polynomial certificate criterion are proved, including square-zero lifts and successive nilpotent lifts over arbitrary coefficient rings."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD5",
      "block_sha256": "427eaa819827ad62fb76e9a32f3281f5260d933ed4ff29664b4aec8639c77b40",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Compatible formally smooth lifts give a genuine completion section. The Rees-module proof of Artin–Rees, exactness of completion on finite modules, tensor identification and ideal flatness criterion are valid for every ideal of the Noetherian polynomial ring; no separatedness or Jacobson-radical assumption is inserted. The resulting quotient is an actual R0-module retract."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD6",
      "block_sha256": "1ab1c6f62263df6b6f21f05af49d5bd504d5bef654cee5b40ab99452f79cbaec",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The formula j([v])=q(v−Phi Psi v) respects both defining relation families, and p j=1; this supplies flatness without asserting descent of the original projective module."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD7",
      "block_sha256": "61ff8e670cbe421fb8322a0a817bd6037400f4e1f895a487bd784463b77226c2",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "One finitely generated subring of the original ring contains every finite certificate. Injective coefficientwise inclusion preserves substitution, matrix identities and all integer homogeneous degrees, including negative degrees and the zero ring."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD8",
      "block_sha256": "0708a57cef49c412e353b1f3470a977d11c6c15048760a2a6231071ee175a5c6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Full original exists_noetherian_subring_homogeneous_matrix_flat_charts: every supplied chart is handled by one prior coefficient ring and one homogeneous matrix; the original ring need not be Noetherian, reduced or flat over the model."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD9",
      "block_sha256": "8527e5bc30ce7579683738175a6d0574f79921f5ac21225c0f10a7acac28b094",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Finite-support degree recurrence proves regularity of X−1, power annihilation of homogeneous elements divisible by X−1, and homogenization modulo X−1 without assuming X regular."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD10",
      "block_sha256": "4de421ef6e63ae505e58a2629b55be2bd6d236f9f697076e249de6276b7b7cbd",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Finite chart generators become one homogeneous family with elementwise power-span properties, including empty chart index sets."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD11",
      "block_sha256": "0fbbf4c71458bb4e0e46583728b45076582a500da8e20dfb2d8e4fa9b58d64a9",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Both exact kernel identities J=K+uF and K intersect uF=uK are proved; finite relation quotients need no Noetherian hypothesis or finite presentation of the source module."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD12",
      "block_sha256": "c9a39f56f399c1299d0cbac05bb182577596918e7b859af10083e2b4d5588aeb",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Full original graded saturating presentation, with homogeneous relation columns and both kernel/cokernel power assertions for every element on each chart; no global finite-generation assumption on G."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD13",
      "block_sha256": "2450687ed5fd2dcc5f04123a9b0deca9b7dcba301959d5368c3df4543d015965",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Actual semilinear dehomogenization has kernel (X−1)G; finite presentation over the polynomial ring follows from explicit lifted B-relations and chart-kernel generators."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD14",
      "block_sha256": "45f0217f638063eff1b34789b1c85ff5d83bb80b58adb58995db3c43e20a1d80",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Original wider scope retained: pi need not be surjective, and only the domain has to carry a direct-sum grading; the target homogeneous-piece condition suffices for the displayed proof."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD15",
      "block_sha256": "142d524c39606589cee04bdd030b4ed80cf458a5a9199a70de7db5e8dc83f7a6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Laurent monomial decomposition, signed contracting homotopy, finite all-negative top classes, descending induction for finite graded modules, and the separate ordinary-Cech degree-zero sequence are correct, including empty index sets."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD16",
      "block_sha256": "4d61eaccb020af18c2d42dfb9c55ed46624070d98e08efe4ca40f74f9d51447d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The actual singleton localization quotient isomorphism, degree shifts, filtered localization and homogeneous direct summands give flatness at every containing nonempty vertex."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD17",
      "block_sha256": "4ddede69bc97f650a153d75eb552e53ab20714fa6ff59650487ffee1573e3bf8",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Cokernel right exactness gives the coefficient comparison under arbitrary nonflat maps; localization and split graded pieces commute with tensor product. Formula-level restriction compatibility supplies one cube map rather than unrelated vertex isomorphisms."
    },
    {
      "id": "FCD18",
      "block_sha256": "6e91b483b2bdbe75d4048a366b47066616ef22725bf501ebd70b84c66095e5b6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Full original noetherian grCube model: one R0, C0=C(coker Phi0,0), and the specified composite theta supply all three outputs. Flatness and bijectivity are required only at nonempty vertices; finite ordinary Cech cohomology holds in every nonnegative degree. Actual geometric section producers remain separate."
    }
